From 5c7ce5f0a42a384b03b405b7229439afd5449126 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:35:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Late-game stone and item evolutions, Trainer Tower type
 summaries (R21)

- trainer_evolutions.py (second pass): Lv. 50+ trainer Pokemon take their
  classic Gen 1-3 stone, item, trade and friendship evolutions (55
  Pokemon: Kingdra, Crobat, Steelix, Blissey, Raichu, ...). Later-gen
  evolutions are left alone.
- validate.py: flags those too.
- Spoiler guide: each Trainer Tower challenge lists the types you'll face.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JQmLEZftLdDmGYX3wiQ71G
---
 HACK_NOTES.md                    |  12 ++-
 include/hack_version.h           |   2 +-
 src/data/trainer_parties.h       | 152 ++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 tools/hack/spoiler_guide.py      |  15 ++-
 tools/hack/trainer_evolutions.py |  30 ++++--
 tools/hack/validate.py           |  13 ++-
 6 files changed, 157 insertions(+), 67 deletions(-)

diff --git a/HACK_NOTES.md b/HACK_NOTES.md
index 8bce5ee..8c7c7f9 100644
--- a/HACK_NOTES.md
+++ b/HACK_NOTES.md
@@ -556,7 +556,11 @@ teams are:
 - **Late-game evolutions:** every trainer Pokémon of Lv. 50 or higher has
   evolved where its level allows (5 levels past the evolution), even if the
   team already has one, e.g. no more Lv. 72 Mareep or Lv. 68 Magikarp.
-  Earlier trainers keep their classic unevolved Pokémon.
+  They also have their classic stone, item, trade and friendship
+  evolutions (Kingdra, Crobat, Steelix, Blissey, Raichu and so on). The
+  later-generation ones (Rhyperior, Magnezone, ...) are left alone, since
+  those items are badge-gated. Earlier trainers keep their classic
+  unevolved Pokémon.
 - **Held items:** the Trainer Tower lobby shop on Seven Island also sells the
   held items competitive teams use: Leftovers, Choice Band, Shell Bell, Focus
   Band, Quick Claw, Scope Lens, Bright Powder, King's Rock, Lucky Egg, Metal
@@ -588,7 +592,8 @@ Each script runs once against the original pret data:
 - `validate.py`: checks the game data for missing or inconsistent entries,
   including that every peak team is six Lv. 100 Pokémon, every Trainer
   Tower team is fully evolved with no repeated species or item, and no
-  Lv. 50+ trainer Pokémon is left unevolved.
+  Lv. 50+ trainer Pokémon is left unevolved (level-up or classic
+  stone/item/trade/friendship evolutions).
 - `playtest/playtest.py [check ...]`: automated playtest. It runs 25 milestone
   checks in a headless mGBA:
   - The boot menu.
@@ -614,7 +619,8 @@ Each script runs once against the original pret data:
   `gcc -O2 -w -o tools/hack/playtest/harness tools/hack/playtest/harness.c -lmgba`.
 - `held_item_shop.py`: held items in the Trainer Tower lobby shop and their prices.
 - `postgame_levels.py`: Sevii Islands 4–7 trainers and wild Pokémon, and post-game route rematches.
-- `trainer_evolutions.py`: Lv. 50+ trainer Pokémon evolve where their level allows (run after `postgame_levels.py`).
+- `trainer_evolutions.py`: Lv. 50+ trainer Pokémon evolve where their level allows, then
+  (second run) by classic stone, item, trade or friendship evolutions (run after `postgame_levels.py`).
 - `tower_sets.py <dir>`: the competitive Trainer Tower teams, from Showdown's
   random-battle set files (read as data).
 - `gym_doubles.py`: the gym double battles (one trainer per gym) and their doubles movesets.
